1075 #edb/ref 17592186434298 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434310 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434310 1077 "selection" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434310 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434288 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434310 1079 #uuid "bada2b14-8923-50b6-a578-2ff2688ef53f" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434311 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434294 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434311 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434311 1077 "field-1" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434311 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434294 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434311 1079 #uuid "c283c6a1-cc2d-5b83-baa1-16866a708164" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434296 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434299 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434300 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434302 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1075 #edb/ref 17592186434306 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1077 "selection" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1078 #edb/ref 17592186434296 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434312 1079 #uuid "fc1ebd9a-4d55-5ce2-ab52-fd21dda2062f" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434313 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434310 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434313 1069 "q-92783" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434313 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434313 1071 "![](images/1f/1f62f15382a5f5d91ea1e2f56acc973d009316f62bdfd70f61fe131a28e42da1.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of rhombuses to the total number of shapes?" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434313 1072 #uuid "2c30cede-8611-5f0a-ae18-9d59bfca44eb" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434313 1074 "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $4$ rhombuses.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $8$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of rhombuses to total shapes is $4:8.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,4 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,8 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rhombuses to the total shapes is $1:2.$" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434314 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434309 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434314 1069 "q-101458" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434314 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434314 1071 "![](images/2f/2fd396c9a62f29969acd4af3de44ac59dd4851a31b77e0c7902ab2e023942e31.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of heptagons to squares is $1:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there is $1$ heptagon for every $\\boxed{}$ squares." 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434314 1072 #uuid "8b912b09-6665-5b0d-812c-febdf9d9cbee" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434314 1074 "First, we count the number of heptagons. We see that there are $4$ heptagons.\n\nThen, we count the number of squares. We see that there are $4$ squares.\n\nSo the ratio of heptagons to squares is $4:4.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,4 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $1:1$ is equivalent to $4:4.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of heptagons to squares is $1:1$ because there is $1$ heptagon for every $1$ square.\"" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434315 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434311 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434315 1069 "q-236318" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434315 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434315 1071 "The ratio $9:2$ is equivalent to the ratio $36:${{field-1}}." 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434315 1072 #uuid "9df9f344-2897-5bbd-9091-a42a8b5a698c" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434315 1074 "To find the ratio equivalent to $9:2$, we multiply both numbers by the same value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,9 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  &  &  & \\,\\,↓\\times \\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,36 &  & : &  & \\,\\boxed{} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get $36$ from $9,$ we multiply $9$ by $4.$ So, to get $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ from $2,$ we multiply $2$ by $4$ as well:\n\n$$\n4\\times 2=8\n$$\n\nThe ratio $9:2$ is equivalent to $36:8.$" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434316 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434307 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434316 1069 "q-236323" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434316 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434316 1071 "The ratio $12:15$ is equivalent to the ratio{{field-1}}$:5.$" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434316 1072 #uuid "d90a8def-3584-5231-870a-71215d7b2ac3" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434316 1074 "To find a ratio that's equivalent to $12:15,$ we divide both numbers by the same value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,12 &  & : & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,15 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\boxed{} &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get $5$ from $15,$ we divide $15$ by $3.$ So, to get $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ from $12,$ we divide $12$ by $3$ as well:\n\n$$\n12÷3=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12:15$ is equivalent to $4:5.$" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434317 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434312 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434317 1069 "q-101451" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434317 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434317 1071 "![](images/79/79b659403c088680490bf308191be82b4acde242292210d15c1fb8525c7addfb.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of squares to the total number of shapes?" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434317 1072 #uuid "f79f6f3f-0665-5958-9f52-a760bcfd2aa5" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434317 1074 "We count the number of squares. We see that there are $3$ squares.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $9$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of circles to total shapes is $3:9.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,9 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,3 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of squares to the total shapes is $1:3.$" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434318 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434308 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434318 1069 "q-59907" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434318 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434318 1071 "A total of $25$ children and $10$ adults gathered for a charity event. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of children to adults is $5:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there were $5$ children for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ adults." 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434318 1072 #uuid "f982038d-d23d-5345-b398-01e403a579af" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true] [17592186434318 1074 "Since there are $25$ children and $10$ adults, the ratio of children to adults is $25:10.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,25 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,10 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,5 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,5 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,5 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $5:2$ is equivalent to $25:10.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of children to adults is $5:2\\,$ because there were $5$ children for every $2\\,$ adults.\"\n\nHence, the missing number is $2.$" 13194139534728 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0462ac67-14b3-5481-a443-957e97903cf8" 17592186434285 "answer-05bfa6a3-b567-5a5f-afbb-e5591b3e1ac6" 17592186434286 "answer-189ca1fc-d9bf-54e1-943e-8d472270ae3f" 17592186434287 "answer-25b4050d-2855-552a-a59b-c2b4ec9e988f" 17592186434288 "answer-26f3ce87-0441-5aab-b938-80ad045e3822" 17592186434289 "answer-2eb20220-add6-5735-a22a-3c908dc65462" 17592186434290 "answer-3419e825-6be0-56a4-9846-a9e56e53ce7e" 17592186434291 "answer-34265f22-1ee0-5927-9535-d8bf181bf917" 17592186434292 "answer-559ac78e-6367-5791-96ba-fc42656ba60a" 17592186434293 "answer-5e64d548-40b5-52fc-b453-675de41c693a" 17592186434294 "answer-70c57267-c777-58cf-bf67-28641d3fbfe3" 17592186434295 "answer-72e3a14a-66f5-5604-b9c3-603dffacd9c6" 17592186434296 "answer-821f0810-2be9-5e28-9ed8-277a2618152b" 17592186434297 "answer-82572c7f-fe5e-5117-809e-0c1f1b0a3a0e" 17592186434298 "answer-8d7094a9-1172-5feb-b8cf-096197051ca5" 17592186434299 "answer-a5b648bc-a24c-5285-b13f-ad7aa8987e7a" 17592186434300 "answer-b242725a-ea8d-51d0-8958-60c3bc36261b" 17592186434301 "answer-b67ea84b-1222-5e4a-9ad1-d45c639a06fd" 17592186434302 "answer-b8727138-94be-5acc-8375-9ebb39076999" 17592186434303 "answer-cdb525e0-c07f-5b8c-a480-6c5f71a051bf" 17592186434304 "answer-d10c19cc-191b-5964-b066-73bf47f80d67" 17592186434305 "answer-e1a1b394-947b-5e5a-b6f9-9a12d5bb161b" 17592186434306 "answer-field-463c8835-db00-5463-a324-96a495b622bf" 17592186434307 "answer-field-51a6d4ad-11fe-5694-8867-69ac29e5267d" 17592186434308 "answer-field-7a6dbb0b-b7b9-5f4e-9215-0a4dfc3abd68" 17592186434309 "answer-field-bada2b14-8923-50b6-a578-2ff2688ef53f" 17592186434310 "answe